{"ok":true,"data":"Editor test case T9_PushCompactHintOnNormalBook \ndescription: switching the compact view on for the editor (as Push Editor Hints does) shows an alert of a normal book as one line, a threshold as name = value, and a channel unchanged \nbefore: alert book Ops \n  channel pager -> pager://ops \n  threshold cpuLimit = 95 \n  <cell muted alert HighCpu [high] when cpu > 90> \nresult: alert book Ops \n  channel pager -> pager://ops \n  threshold cpuLimit = 95 \n  muted alert HighCpu [high] when cpu > 90 \ncode: \n  EditorComponent ec = editor component; \n  Assert.assertFalse(\"default view before the switch\", Arrays.asList(\"muted\", \"alert\", \"HighCpu\", \"[\", \"high\", \"]\").equals(CompactViewTestUtil.memberLabels(ec, \"HighCpu\"))); \n  CompactViewTestUtil.pushCompact(ec); \n  Assert.assertEquals(Arrays.asList(\"muted\", \"alert\", \"HighCpu\", \"[\", \"high\", \"]\"), CompactViewTestUtil.memberLabels(ec, \"HighCpu\")); \n  Assert.assertFalse(\"compact alert shows no condition\", CompactViewTestUtil.isChildShown(ec, \"HighCpu\", \"condition\")); \n  Assert.assertEquals(Arrays.asList(\"cpuLimit\", \"=\", \"95\"), CompactViewTestUtil.memberLabels(ec, \"cpuLimit\")); \n  Assert.assertEquals(Arrays.asList(\"channel\", \"pager\", \"->\", \"pager://ops\"), CompactViewTestUtil.memberLabels(ec, \"pager\"));"}

